      "id": "streams.consumer_group_round_trip",
      "model": "streams",
      "why": "NEW, found by this suite on 2026-08-13 and in no prior finding list. xadd returns an entry id as a string ('1786606665529-0'), and xack's signature is (stream, group, id_ms: int, id_seq: int). The client cannot feed its own xadd output back into its own xack — the natural round trip does not typecheck, so the consumer-group surface has never been usable end to end from Python. Not one of the 18 known never-worked shapes.",
      "xfail": {
        "reason": "xack takes (id_ms, id_seq) integers while xadd returns a single 'ms-seq' string. The two halves of the same API do not compose."
