    {
      "id": "sql.scalar_jsonb_parameter",
      "model": "sql",
      "why": "NEW and the most severe thing this suite has found. `SELECT $1::jsonb` over the EXTENDED protocol describes the statement as returning ZERO result columns and then executes it returning one, so a strict client (asyncpg, and by construction pgx and JDBC) aborts with a protocol error. This is the same defect class as the 18 known never-worked shapes, except it is plain SQL rather than a specialty function — which means it is not a gap in a Nucleus extension, it is a gap in 'any PostgreSQL client works'. psql does not catch it because psql does not validate the described column count against the row it receives, and because \\bind is answered by substituting the parameter into the query text.",
      "issue": "P11",
      "steps": [
        {
          "op": "sql.queryScalar",
          "args": [
            "SELECT $1::jsonb",
            [
              "{\"a\":1}"
            ]
          ],
          "expect": {
            "jsonDecode": true,
            "equals": {
              "a": 1
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
